    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0413" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/87: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-26T22:00:00-05:00">September 26, 1940—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Reference telephone conversation Satterthwaite<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d462-f1"/> this afternoon. Minister for Foreign Affairs states
                    Colombia requested quota of 3,180,000 bags instead of 3,150,000 not as a matter
                    of quantity but because Congress expected 3,200,000 and may be unwilling to
                    approve any greater cut. However, he will see the President tonight and
                    communicate with me in the morning before I leave for Panama.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d462-f1" n="15" xml:id="d462-f1-content">
                <p>Livingston Satterthwaite, of the Division of the American Republics.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
